� �����������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n������� ����� ��������� ������� ���������� ���� ������������������ ������������������ ����������\n������� ���������������� �������� ��� ����������� ������� ������� ��� ������ ���������� ���������\n��������� ���� ����������� ���� ���� ������������� ���������������� ��������������� �������������� ���������������� ���������������\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��� �������� ��� ������� ���������� ����� ��� ���������� ������� �������� �� �������������� ����\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�����������������������������\n���� ����������������� ��� ����� ���������� �� ��������� ��� ����������� ��������� ���������� ����\n�������������������������������������������������������������������\n������\n�\n�"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|7|UNSTARRED |111", "t": "LHB Coaches", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.111 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 24.02.2016 \n \nLHB COACHES \n \n111. SHRI SHRIRANG APPA BARNE: \n        SHRI ANANDRAO ADSUL:  \n        SHRI DHARMENDRA YADAV:  \n        SHRI P.R. SUNDARAM:  \n        SHRI ADHALRAO PATIL SHIVAJIRAO: \n \n  Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Railways took a decision to replace the conventional AC and \nnon-AC coaches with new Linke Hofmann Busch (LHB) coaches in all trains \nby the end of 2016; \n \n(b) if so, whether while passengers complain of rattling and unclean coaches \nin many express/passenger trains, whereas LHB coaches; \n \n(c) if so, the number of coaches procured and number out of them have not \nbeen utilised so far along with the reasons therefor;  \n \n(d) whether the LHB coaches have not been allocated to the zones as per \ntheir size or as per their requirement and if so, the reasons therefor; and \n \n(e) the steps taken by the Government to use these LHB coaches and \nprovide more LHB coaches in high spe ed trains under the Southern \nRailways? \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n(a) No, Madam.  \n \n(b) Does not arise. \n\n \n(c) to (e) About 3300 LHB coaches have been made available from \nproduction units for the purpose of utilization as new service as well as \nreplacement. Production and the allotment of coaches is an ongoing \nprocess. Allocations of LHB coaches to all zonal Railways including Southern \nRailway are being done keeping in view the production, requirement and \ninfrastructure for maintaining LHB coaches available at Zonal Railway.  \n \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|7|UNSTARRED |112", "t": "Skill Training for Poor", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN POVERTY ALLEVIATION \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 112 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON FEBRUARY 24, 2016 \n \nSKILL TRAINING FOR POOR \n \nNo. 112 SHRI S.P.MUDDAHANUME GOWDA:   \n   \nWill the Minister of HOUSING AN D URBAN POVERTY ALLEVIATION \nbe pleased to state:- \n(a) whether the Government is making any efforts through \nimparting skill to make the urban  poor eligible for gainful \nemployment or undertake wage employment; \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n(c) whether the Government is focusing on SCs/STs in urban areas \nso that they can become eligib le for gainful employment or \nundertake wage employment; \n(d) if so, the details thereof; and  \n(e) if not, the reasons therefor? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN  \nTHE MINISTRY OF HOUSING & URBAN POVERTY ALLEVIATION \n[SHRI BABUL SUPRIYO] \n  \n(a) & (b): The Ministry of Housing and Urban Poverty \nAlleviation is implementing a Centrally Sponsored Scheme \n“Deendayal Antyodaya Yojana — National Urban Livelihoods \nMission”. The Employment through Skill Training & Placement \n(EST&P) component of the Missi on aims at providing skill \ntraining to urban poor so that they can find gainful \nemployment or set up self-emp loyment ventures or secure \nwage employment.   \n(c)  to (e): As per Mission guide lines, SCs and ST s are to be \nbenefited at least to the exten t of the proportion of their \npopulation in the city. \n****** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|7|UNSTARRED |113", "t": "Setting up of Rail Coach Factory", "head": " \n \n                                          GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \n                                         MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n                      LOK SABHA \n                                    UNSTARRED QUESTION NO.113 \n                                   TO BE ANSWERED ON 24.02.2016 \n \n \n                        SETTING UP OF RAIL COACH FACTORY \n \n   113. SHRI RAJESH KUMAR DIWAKER: \n    \n   Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n    \n(a) whether the  Railways proposes to set up a rail coach factory in Hathras \n(UP); \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof;     \n \n(c) the funds required for setting up the said factory along with the pattern of \nits funding; \n \n(d) whether necessary clearances have been obtained for the project from the \nState Government and other agencies and if so, the details thereof and \nresponse of State; \n \n(e) whether the site of the factory has been identified and land allotted for the \npurpose; and \n \n(f) if not, the time by which it is likely to be allotted and which type of coaches \nproposes to be manufactured in the said factory? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n                                      (SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n(a) No, Madam. \n \n(b)  to (f) Do not arise. \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|7|UNSTARRED |114", "t": "CNG Powered Trains", "head": "  GOVERMENT OF INDIA \n MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n          LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION N0. 114 \n   TO BE ANSWERED ON 24.02.2016 \n \nCNG POWERED TRAINS \n \n114.  SHRI SUSHIL KUMAR SINGH: \n \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n (a)  whether the Government intends to run Compressed Natural Gas \n(CNG) powered trains in various parts of the country; \n \n(b)   if so, the details thereof; \n \n(c) whether result of pilot project taken in Ahmedabad for CNG powered \ntrains has been found workable; and \n \n(d) if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n (a)  Yes, Madam.  \n (b) (i)  Railways have sanctioned conversion of 100 Nos. of driving power \ncar (DPC) of Diesel Electric Multiple Unit (DEMU) into dual fuel with \nCompressed Natural Gas (CNG). \n (ii) Eleven CNG powered DPCs are working at Shakurbasti based DEMU \nrakes operative on Northern Railway and North Western Railway. \n(c)&(d) No, Madam.  Such pilot project has not been taken up in \nAhmedabad for CNG powered trains. \n****** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|7|UNSTARRED |115", "t": "MoU between India and France", "head": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION  NO.115 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 24.02.2016 \n \n \nMOU BETWEEN INDIA AND FRANCE \n \n \nϯ115.        SHRI  RAMDAS C. TADAS: \n \n      \n \n Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n \n \n(a)   whether any Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) has been signed \nbetween the India and France for the modernisation of railway stations \nand development of various rail projects in the country; \n \n(b)   if so, the details thereof; \n \n(c)   whether the Government has taken any effective steps to complete \nthe pending railway projects particularly rural rail projects on priority \nbasis and if so, the details thereof; and \n \n(d) the number of such pending rail projects in Maharashtra which are \nproposed to be started in the current year till date? \n \nANSWER \n \n \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n \n \n \n \n    (SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n \n \n(a) & (b):  Ministry of Railways have signed a Memorandum of \nUnderstanding (MoU) with SNCF( Societe Nationale des Chemins de Fer \nFrancais), the French  National Railways, on 14th  February 2013 in \nwhich the agreed areas of cooperation are : (i) High Speed and semi-high \nspeed rail; (ii) Station renovation and operations; (iii) Modernization of \ncurrent operations and infrastructure; and (iv) Suburban trains. \n…2.. \n \n\n-2- \n \n(c): Completion of projects depends on many factors such as land \nacquisition, forestry & wild life clearances, shifting of services, \nconstruction of road over and road under bridges by road maintaining \nagencies etc. apart from availability of  funds. Railways have increased \noutlay for projects like new lines, gauge conversion and doubling \nsubstantially in last 2 years which has increased pace of project \nexecution. \n \n  (d):   In 2015-16, two new line projects viz. Karad -Chiplun (112 km) \nand Dighi Port –Roha (34 km) have been included in Railway Budget. In \naddition, 7 doubling projects covering a length of 1377 km. that fall \nfully/partly in the State of Maharashtra have been sanctioned in 2015 -16 \nsubject to requisite clearances. \n \n******* \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|7|UNSTARRED |116", "t": "Mobile Production", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF LAW AND JUSTICE\nDEPARTMENT OF JUSTICE\nLOK SABHA\nSTARRED QUESTION NO. †*116\nTO BE ANSWERED ON THURSDAY, 03RD MARCH, 2016\nInfrastructure for Judiciary\n†*116. SHRIMATI RAMA DEVI:\nSHRI ASADUDDIN OWAISI:\nWill the Minister of LAW AND JUSTICE be pleased to state:\n(a) whether the Government has any mechanism to monitor and ensure that the \nfunds released to various States under Centrally Sponsored Scheme (CSS) for \nthe development of infrastructure facilities for judiciary are utilised for the \npurpose within a stipulated time-frame;\n(b) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor;\n(c) the details of States which have not submitted utilisation certificates for the \nfunds released by the Union Government for the purpose during each of the \nlast three years and the current year, State / UT-wise;\n(d) whether the Government has urged various State Governments including \nAndhra Pradesh and Telangana to submit the utilisation certificates which have \nbecome overdue and if so, the details thereof; and\n(e) the other measures taken / being taken by the Government to grant more funds \nto States where the requisite infrastructure is lacking?\nANSWER\nMINISTER OF LAW AND JUSTICE\n(SHRI D. V. SADANANDA GOWDA)\n(a) to (e): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House.\n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) to (e) of LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *116 FOR ANSWER ON 03rd March, 2016.\nThe development of infrastructure facilities for judiciary is the primary responsibility \nof the State Governments.  However, in order to augment the resources of the State \nGovernments, a Centrally Sponsored Scheme (CSS) for development of infrastructure \nfacilities for judiciary has been in operation since 1993-94.  \nThe progress of infrastructure development for judiciary in States is monitored by a \ncommittee chaired by the portfolio judge of the High Court as per the directions of the\nSupreme Court in All India Judges Association cases (I.A. No.279 in W.P. (C) No.1022 of \n1989).  In the Joint Conference of Chief Ministers and Chief Justices held on 07 th April \n2013, it was, inter-alia, decided that the mechanism created by the Supreme Court of \nDistrict and State Committees be made a permanent feature and the Chief Justices of \nHigh Courts should actively utilise the said mechanism for ensuring timely proposals for \ncreation, furnishing, maintenance and development of infrastructure of Court buildings and \nresidences.\nThe details of funds sanctioned to the State Governments and Union Territories\nduring the last three years and the current year and funds for which Utilisation Certificates \nhave become due but not yet received from State Governments / Union Territories, have \nbeen indicated in the Statement annexed.  State Governments are reminded from time to \ntime to submit pending Utilisation Certificates.  The State Governments of Andhra Pradesh \nand Telegana have also been reminded in this regard. On receipt of the complete \nproposals from the State Governments including utilisation certificates for the funds \nsanctioned earlier, further financial assistance is sanctioned in terms of the guidelines of \nthe Scheme and subject to availability of funds.\nOn account of the recommendations of the Fourteenth Finance Commission, there \nhas been a substantial increase in devolution of funds to the State Governments.  The \nCentral Government has, therefore, written to the State Governments to utilize the \nadditional fiscal space available to them for enhancing the investment on judiciary in the \nStates.\n**************\n\nAnnexure\nStatement referred to Lok Sabha Starred Question No. *116 for Reply on 03.03.2016\nDetails of Funds Sanctioned to the State Governments and Union Territories during \nthe last three years and funds for which Utilisation Certificates have become due \nbut not yet received.\n(Rs. in Lakhs)\nSl. \nNo.\nState / UT Funds \nSanctioned \nin 2012-13\nFunds \nSanctioned \nin 2013-14\nFunds \nSanctioned \nin 2014-15\nFunds \nSanctioned \nin 2015-16\nTotal amount for \nwhich Utilization\nCertificate due but \nnot yet received.\n1. Andhra Pradesh\nincluding Telengana\n6393.00 0.00 0.00 0.00 4516.00\n2. Bihar 1524.00 0.00 4909.35 0.00 90.65\n3. Chhattisgarh 0.00 0.00 2176.60 0.00 132.00\n4. Goa 0.00 0.00 0.00 0.00 125.87\n5. Gujarat 9893.00 10000.00 10000.00 5000.00 0.00\n6. Haryana 0.00 3632.00 0.00 5000.00 0.00\n7. Himachal Pradesh 0.00 806.00 0.00 0.00 0.00\n8. Jammu & Kashmir 2572.00 3428.00 3429.00 1325.00 0.00\n9. Jharkhand 1500.00 1693.00 3044.00 3044.00 0.00\n10. Karnataka 7610.00 10384.00 16370.00 5000.00 0.00\n11. Kerala 1499.00 0.00 0.00 0.00 490.95\n12. Madhya Pradesh 2046.00 6141.00 6141.00 5000.00 0.00\n13. Maharashtra 5920.24 10000.00 9975.00 5000.00 0.00\n14. Orissa 1534.00 0.00 0.00 0.00 2247.18\n15. Punjab 7902.00 12000.00 9805.00 5000.00 0.00\n16. Rajasthan 1042.00 0.00 0.00 5000.00 0.00\n17. Tamilnadu 1953.00 7343.00 0.00 0.00 2962.91\n18. Uttarakhand 829.76 2043.00 3559.05 0.00 283.40\n19. Uttar Pradesh 9398.00"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|7|UNSTARRED |117", "t": "ISDS in Textile Sector", "head": "������������������� �\n�������������������������������������������������� �\n�\n��������� �\n�\n������������������������������ �\n�������������������� ����������������� �\n�\n�����������������������\n�\n�������� �\n�\n����������������������� �\n���� �\n�������� ���� ��������� ��� ������ ������������ ���� ����������������� ���\n������������������\n�\n���� �������� ���� ����������� ���� ���������� ���� ��������� ���� ���� ����������� � ���������\n���������������������������������������������\n����\n���� ������� ���� ����������� �������� ���� ���� �������� ��� ����������� ���� ������������� �����\n�����������������������������������\n�\n�����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��� �\n������\n���������������������������������������������\n�\n������ �\n�\n�\n����������������������������������������������������������������\n�������������������������������� �\n������������������������ �\n�\n�\n����������� ���� ��������� ��� ������������� ���������� �� ��������� ��������� ���\n���������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n���������� ��� ���� ��������� ���� ��� ��������� ���� ������������� ��� ���� ������� ����\n������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n������������������������������������������������������������������������ �� ��\n�\n� �����������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�������������������������� ����������������