NISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS\n(SHRI HARIBHAI PARATHIBHAI CHAUDHARY)\n(a) to (c): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House.\n******\n\n-2-\nSTATEMENT IN REPLY TO THE LOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION NO.*148\nFOR 08.03.2016.\n(a): The total number of cases reported, cases charge sheeted, cases\nconvicted, cases conviction rate, persons arrested, persons charge\nsheeted and persons convicted under the Protection of Children from\nSexual Offences(POCSO) Act, 2012 during 2014 is enclosed at Annexure-I.\nAs NCRB has started collecting the data since 2014, no data is available\nfor 2013. Data for the year 2015 is being collected by NCRB.\n(b): The Protection of Children from Sexual offences Act, 2012 came into\nforce on 14.11.2012. The Act has been in force since the last three years.\nTherefore a review is not planned at this stage. On 14.01.2016, Ministry of\nWomen & Child Development and National Commission for Protection of\nChild Rights (NCPCR) jointly held a consultation with all stakeholders\nresponsible for implementing the POCSO Act. During the consultation it\nwas emphasized that there is a need for dissemination of information,\ncreation of awareness and registration of cases under POCSO Act.\n(c): No separate budget is allocated for the implementation of POCSO\nAct.\n*******\n\nPAGE 1 OF 1 OF ANNEXURE-I\nL.S.S.Q.NO.*148 FOR 8.3.2016\nCases Reported(CR), Cases Chargesheeted (CCS), Cases Compounded or Withdrawn (CCW), Cases in which Trials were Completed (CTC), Cases Convicted (CON),\nConviction Rate (CVR), Persons Arrested (PART), Persons Charge Sheeted (PCST), Persons Convicted  (PCVT), Persons Acquitted (PAQT), Persons Discharged by Court\n(PDIST) under  The Protection of Children from Sexual Offences Act, 2012  During 2014\nSl.No. States/UTs CR CCS CCW CTC CON CVR PART PCST PCVT PAQT PDIST\n1 Andhra Pradesh 106 52 0 17 1 5.9 113 83 1 40 0\n2 Arunachal Pradesh 5 3 0 0 0 - 6 3 0 0 0\n3 Assam 311 141 0 5 5 100.0 308 141 5 0 0\n4 Bihar 57 46 0 10 4 40.0 72 58 6 6 0\n5 C