sed to state: \n(a) whether it is true that the timely detection of a bomb by an alert \npatrol party minutes before departure of a passenger train averted \na major tragedy in Farrukhabad railway station; \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n(c) whether it is also true that the Railways is r eceiving hoax calls \nregarding bomb on board of many trains in the recent past; and  \n(d) if so, the details thereof? \n \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n       ( SHRI MANOJ SINHA ) \n \n(a) to (d):    A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n***** \n \n  \n\n \nSTATEMENT REFERRE D TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO ( d) OF \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.  149 BY DR. P. VENUGOPAL TO BE \nANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 24.02.2016 REGARDING DETECTION OF \nBOMB AT FARRUKHABAD RAILWAY STATION. \n \n(a) and (b) :  Yes, Madam. On 03.10.2015  at 06.10 hrs , one Improvised \nExplosive Device was found near parcel office of Farrukhabad Railway \nStation. The bomb was defused by the Police Bomb D isposal squad at \n13.10 hrs.  No loss of property or life was reported due to the incident. \nIn this connecti on, Government Railway Police/Farrukhabad registered \na case vide Cr. No. 36/15 u/s 03/04 of Explosive Substance Act, 1908 on \n03.10.2015. \n \n(c) and (d) : Yes, Madam. The details of hoax calls regarding bomb on \nboard trains received during the years 201 3, 201 4 and 2015  are as \nunder:-  \n \nYear Number of hoax calls received regarding  bomb on \nboard trains  \n2013 21 \n2014 34 \n2015 103 \n \n \n**** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|7|UNSTARRED |15", "t": "Entry of Private Companies", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 15 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 24.02.2016 \n \nENTRY OF PRIVATE COMPANIES \n \n \n15.   SHRI KAUSHALENDRA KUMAR:  \n \n  Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the NITI Aayog  member has recommended for the entry of \nprivate companies in many core areas of Indian Railways; \n \n(b) if so, whether the Government has accepted these \nrecommendations; and \n \n(c) if so, the details thereof?  \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n \n(a): A Committee for Mobilisation of Resources for Major Railway \nProjects and Restructuring of Railway Ministry & Railway Board \nheaded by Dr. Bibek Debroy , currently a NITI Aayog Member , in its \nreport submitted in June, 2015, had inter -alia, recommended entry of \nprivate companies in: \n \n●   Manufacture of rolling stock. \n● On -board catering through large food chains and local \nrestaurants. \n--2/- \n\n-2- \n●  Leasing  of parcel vans in trains through auction of carrying \ncapacity. \n●   Private Parcel Trains and Concessioning of train services. \n \n(b) & (c): Manufacture of rolling stock through private sector has \nalready been allowed. On -board catering has also been implemented \nby Indian Railway Catering and Tourism Corporation (IRCTC). Leasing \nof Parcel Vans has been going on for some years. At present, there is \nno proposal to allow private players in operation of passenger train \nservices. \n \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|7|UNSTARRED |150", "t": "Upgrading ITIs", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF FOOD PROCESSING INDUSTRIES \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.*150 \nANSWERED ON 8TH MARCH, 2016 \n \nFOOD PROCESSING \n*150. SHRI RAJENDRA AGRAWAL: \n         Will the Minister of FOOD PROCESSING INDUSTRIES be pleased to state: \n(a) whether the contribution of the Food Processing Sector (FPS) to the Gross \nDomestic Product (GDP) is rising over the years; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof during the last three years and the current year; \n \n(c) whether any target has been set to create employment opportuni ties in the  Food \nProcessing Sector and increase its share in GDP;  and \n \n(d) if so, the details thereof and the steps taken to achieve the said targets? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR FOOD PROCESSING INDUSTRIES \n(SADHVI NIRANJAN JYOTI) \n \n(a)  to (d):     A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) to (d) OF LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.  *150 FOR ANSWER ON 8 TH MARCH, 2016 \nREGARDING FOOD PROCESSING \n \n(a)& (b):  As per the information provided by Central Statistics Office, Ministry of \nStatistics and Programme Implementation, the percentage share of Gross \nValue Added (GVA) from food processing in total GVA at current prices \nis as follows: \nYear Share of GVA from Food \nProcessing Industries (%) \n2011-12 1.81 \n2012-13 1.54 \n2013-14 1.44 \n2014-15 1.43 \n \n \n(c) & (d): To create employment opportunities in the food processing sector and \nincrease its share in GDP, the Ministry of Food Processing Industries is \nimplementing Schemes of Mega Food Parks, Cold Chain, Value Addition \nand Preservation Infrastructure, Setting up/ M odernization of Abattoirs \nand Strengthening of Institutions.  \n \n \n***** \n \n \n \n \n \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|7|UNSTARRED |151", "t": "Research Work", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS\nLOK SABHA\nSTARRED QUESTION NO.†*151\nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 8th MARCH, 2016/PHALGUNA 18, 1937 (SAKA)\nDOMESTIC VIOLENCE\n† *151. SHRI RATTAN LAL KATARIA:\nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state:\n(a) the number of criminal cases registered in regard to domestic violence\nagainst women along with the action taken against the guilty during each\nof the last three years and the current year, State-wise;\n(b) whether women are the victims of verbal and psychological abuse in\n75 percent of cases of domestic violence and if so, the details thereof\nalong with the steps taken for appointment of protection officers to deal\nwith the said cases;\n(c) the percentage of cases of physical violence out of the cases of\ndomestic violence registered in the country during the said period;\n(d) the percentage of conviction achieved in the domestic violence cases\nregistered in the country; and\n(e) whether the conviction rate is very low due to lack of coordination\nbetween the prosecution and police and if so, the details in this regard?\nANSWER\nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS\n(SHRI HARIBHAI PARATHIBHAI CHAUDHARY)\n(a) to (e): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House.\n******\n\n-2-\nSTATEMENT IN REPLY TO THE LOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION NO.*151\nFOR 08.03.2016.\n(a): NCRB has started collecting data under the Protection of Women\nfrom Domestic Violence Act 2005 since 2014. State/UT wise cases\nregistered, cases charge sheeted, cases convicted, persons arrested,\npersons charge sheeted and persons convicted under the Protection of\nWomen from Domestic Violence Act 2005 during 2014 is at Annexure-I.\nThe data pertaining to 2015 is being collected by NCRB.\n(b) & (c): The data on percentage of cases of physical violence out of\nDomestic Violence registered in the country is not maintained by NCRB.\nAll State Governments have appointed Protection Officers to deal with\nsuch cases as is mandated under the Protection of Women from Domestic\nViolence Act (PWDVA) 2005.\n(d) & (e): As per the information given by NCRB, the conviction rate is\n19.1% (9 cases convicted out of 47 cases in which trial is completed)\nunder PWDV Act.\n…3/\n\n-3-\nL.S.S.Q.NO.*151 FOR 8.3.2016\nAs per the seventh schedule to the Constitution of India `Police` and\n`Public Order` are State subjects and, as such, the primary responsibility\nof prevention, detection, registration, investigation and prosecution of\ncrime, lies with the State Governments/ Union Territory Administrations.\n*******\n\nPAGE 1 OF 1 OF Annexure – I\nL.S.S.Q.NO.*151 FOR 8.3.2016\nState/UT wise cases registered (CR), cases charge sheeted (CS), cases convicted (CV), cases in which trial completed (TC),\ncases conviction rate (CVR), persons arrested (PAR), persons charge sheeted (PCS) and persons convicted (PCV) under the\nPr